# Task: Fix login bug

## Description

The login page returns a 500 error when the password is empty.

## Ticket

https://example.atlassian.net/browse/TICKET-100

## Repository

https://github.com/org/repo

## Labels

bug, backend

## Instructions

**IMPORTANT: A merge request already exists for this task at:
https://github.com/org/repo/pull/42
Do NOT create a new merge request. Push your commits to the existing branch
and the MR will update automatically.**

1. Configure git globally:
   ```
   git config --global user.name "Osmia"
   git config --global user.email "osmia@localhost"
   git config --global init.defaultBranch main
   # Configure git credentials from SCM token env vars
   if [ -n "${GITLAB_TOKEN:-}" ]; then
     git config --global credential.helper store
     echo "https://oauth2:${GITLAB_TOKEN}@gitlab.com" >> ~/.git-credentials
   fi
   if [ -n "${GITHUB_TOKEN:-}" ]; then
     git config --global credential.helper store
     echo "https://x-access-token:${GITHUB_TOKEN}@github.com" >> ~/.git-credentials
   fi
   ```

2. Clone the repository to /workspace/repo:
   ```
   git clone --depth=1 https://github.com/org/repo /workspace/repo
   ```

3. Create a branch for your changes (use the same branch on every retry so work is not lost):
   ```
   git checkout -b osmia/TICKET-100
   ```

4. Commit and push your changes to that branch at logical checkpoints:
   ```
   git add -A && git commit -m "wip: <short description>"
   git push origin osmia/TICKET-100
   ```

5. An MR already exists — do NOT create another one.
   Simply push your commits to branch `osmia/TICKET-100` and the MR will update automatically.

6. When the full task is complete, write /workspace/result.json containing:
   `{"success": true, "summary": "<one-line summary>", "branch_name": "osmia/TICKET-100", "merge_request_url": "https://github.com/org/repo/pull/42"}`
